LSP servers of extensions keyed by server name

A Claude plugin's .lsp.json is keyed by server name and lists its languages
in extensionToLanguage ({ "mariadb": { "command": ..., "extensionToLanguage":
{ ".sql": "sql" } } }), while the loader read every key as a language and
named the server after its command: /lsp showed the launcher path as the
server and "mariadb" as its language. For configs declared by extensions
that carry an extensionToLanguage mapping, the key is now the server name
and the mapped languages are its languages. A project's own .lsp.json keeps
the language-keyed format.

